    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "## Problem\n\nBased on https://github.com/neovim/deps/pull/24 it seems like we fetch some dependencies from https://github.com/neovim/deps/tree/master/opt because it fit the shape of our `ExternalProject_Add` pattern.\n\nBut if we have to manage dependencies manually in https://github.com/neovim/deps/tree/master/opt , that's not *really* different in terms of maintenance than inlining the code into the Neovim tree itself, assuming:\n\n- the library is \"reasonably small\"\n- the library is rarely updated\n- the library license is compatible with in-tree inclusion (i.e. not GPL)\n\nBenefits:\n\n- maintenance / build steps are more obvious\n\n## Proposal\n\n- eliminate libiconv (?)\n- inline lpeg source to `src/lpeg/` https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/41527\n- inline a [non-GPL version of gettext](https://github.com/neovim/deps/pull/55#issuecomment-5452985413)\n- update MAINTAIN.md\n- delete `opt/` from https://github.com/neovim/deps ",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "* at least on macOS, `libiconv` is taken from the system by default -- maybe we can punt to system libraries on other platforms as well? (The problem is, of course, Windows.)\n* `gettext` includes binary tools; not sure if we use them, in which case inlining doesn't make sense -- possibly we could port them to Lua scripts in that case?\n* we only need to \"out-of-tree vendor\" dependencies on unreliable hosts (GNU ftp servers) or non-standard repositories (Luarocks); as https://github.com/sabotage-linux/gettext-tiny is hosted on Github (like us), there's no such pressure to host this ourselves and can keep it as a standard dependency. (Of course, we may still want to vendor for other reasons.)",
            "created_at": "2026-08-28T14:37:29Z",
